Z||000000||turbo86se||04-03-2000||11:44 AM||||<BR>This morning on my way to school, I notice a silver Fiero entering the highway from the entrance ramp. I speed up and get right behind him. It was a nice silver SE V6 with personalized plates that read: 87FIERO!  I got beside him at a red light as I was turning into my college and gave him a smile and a thumbs up, he did the same! BTW, I was driving my yellow 88 coupe. <BR>On my way out of school, at the same intersection, I was sitting at the red light playing with my stereo and I hear someone honking twice. I look up and a black Fiero GT passed right in front of me! I haven't seen any of these guys before! Where have they been hiding?  ||||reg||7
Z||000001||Motorhead||04-03-2000||03:56 PM||||Maybe the ones we know about are getting together while we sleep, and producing offspring!  I've only seen a couple around the beach in the past year.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||04-03-2000||08:37 PM||||Maybe the Fieros hibernate in the winter like mine do.  In upstate NY they have something called snow and they use salt to remove it and that yields to rust.  So the cars stay off the road until all is clear.||||reg||1
